## Problem classes

### `Compose lint KaCall crash`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `lintDebug` aborts: `Found class …KaFunctionCall, but interface was expected` in Compose runtime detectors | Compose BOM / Compose lint jars newer than Kotlin analysis API bundled with AGP | Align Compose BOM to the AGP+Kotlin generation (e.g. `2024.12.01` with AGP 8.7 / Kotlin 2.0). Disable only the crashing detectors as a temporary bridge — do not bump AGP/Kotlin as a drive-by. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `UI starts VPN directly`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Toggle bypasses AUTO | `MainViewModel` still calls `ZerotierBVpnService.start` | Route all mode changes through orchestrator |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Consent banner flips global mode`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| AUTO + consent-missing banner → user taps Grant → global mode becomes VPN | Banner reused `requestVpnAndStart()` which calls `setGlobalMode(VPN)` | Banner: `requestVpnConsent()` = `VpnService.prepare()` + `orchestrator.refresh()` only; segmented VPN chip keeps full `requestVpnAndStart()` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `M3 Expressive BOM blocked`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| material3 1.5.0-alpha needs AGP 9 / compileSdk 37 | BOM bump on pinned AGP 8.7 | Stay on `compose-bom:2024.12.01`; use stable `SegmentedButton` + `CircularProgressIndicator` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Proxy network row shows em-dash`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Network row `Status: —` while PROXY is up and joined | ViewModel reads only the VPN stack's per-network list; proxy join state lived only inside the libzt node manager | Both runtimes publish `NetworkRuntimeStatus` on their `StateFlow`; ViewModel resolves via `plan.runtime` + `resolveNetworkRuntime` — never hard-wire VPN-only |

